# Remote Qwen endpoint deployed by this directory.
#
# This file is hand-maintained — nothing generates or rewrites it. `pnpm
# deploy` writes only `remote.json`, which carries the deployment state: the
# Lambda URLs `outfit remote` drives and the endpoint's base URL. From this
# directory:
#   outfit remote deploy  # tell the endpoint what to serve (this file + preset)
#   outfit remote start   # boot the instance; prints the OPENAI_API_KEY export
#   outfit apply          # point your coding agent at the endpoint
#   outfit remote stop    # stop now instead of waiting for the idle timer
#
# PROVIDER names the inference engine, so this file is what chooses llama.cpp
# over vLLM: `outfit remote deploy` asks the cloud for that engine, and the same
# file runs it locally under `outfit serve`. To cut back to vLLM, set PROVIDER
# to vllm, drop PRESET, and set MODEL to the FP8 repo (Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B-FP8).
# Either way the deploy Lambda seeds the weights into S3 if they are not there.
#
# ALIAS is both the name your coding agent asks for and the name the server is
# started under (llama-server's --alias), so the two cannot drift apart.
#
# There is deliberately no BASEURL: the endpoint's address belongs to the
# deployment, so `outfit apply` takes it from remote.json's base_url. Add a
# BASEURL here only to override that.
PROVIDER llamacpp
ALIAS    qwen3.6-27b
CONTEXT  131072
PRESET   ./preset.ini
REMOTE   qwen3.6-27b
